  "title": "Meghalaya Mandates Energy Storage for Net Metering Projects of 10 kW",
  "summary": "The Meghalaya State Electricity Regulatory Commission (MSERC) has mandated that distributed renewable energy systems (DRES) over 10 kW under the net metering framework must have a hybrid inverter and a battery energy storage system with a minimum storage capacity equivalent to 20% of the project's daily energy generation potential.The mandate was announced under the state's guidelines installation and operation of grid-interactive DRES.",
